TASK B47
	TITLE "brigade collect runs a collector under one contract, caches its document and ships the"
		+ "built-ins git-log, git-diff-stat, worktrees, corpus and ledger"
	STATUS archived
	DESC "archived on 2026-10-24: @TASK.B206 makes false its SPEC that tests/cli prove a cache hit,"
		+ "--refresh, a failing collector left out of the cache, a collector declaring nothing"
		+ "never cached and each built-in on a fixture repository; those are proven in tests/unit,"
		+ "and tests/cli keeps collect --json, collect inside a run, a failing collector and"
		+ "collectors list as JSON and text"
	MILESTONE @MILESTONE.M1
	COMPONENT "studies"
	ROLE ada
	SPEC "a collector is an executable or a built-in module of brigade/collectors/ that reads"
		+ "BRIGADE_PROJECT_PATH, BRIGADE_SINCE, a date, BRIGADE_RUN_DIR when set and"
		+ "BRIGADE_PARAMS, the key=value pairs as JSON, from its environment and prints one JSON"
		+ "document on stdout; it exits 0 when its document is complete"
		IMPL "brigade/collecting/collector_environment.py::def create_collector_environment(inputs:"
			+ "CollectorInputs) -> dict:"
		IMPL "brigade/system/resolve_collector.py::class ExecutableCollector:"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_collect.py::def"
			+ "test_should_hand_the_collector_the_project_the_since_and_the_parameters(self):"
	SPEC "the document carries schema_version, an integer from 1, collector, collected_at, summary"
		+ "and items, and may carry cache, a boolean by which the collector declares that its"
		+ "document is cached; it is validated against the shape declared beside the kind before"
		+ "brigade reads it; a document that fails validation is a failure of the collector naming"
		+ "the key"
		IMPL "brigade/collecting/collector_shapes.py::COLLECTOR_DOCUMENT_SHAPE = {"
		IMPL "tests/unit/collecting/test_collect_document.py::def"
			+ "test_should_refuse_a_document_outside_the_collector_shape(self):"
		IMPL "tests/unit/system/test_validate_document.py::def"
			+ "test_should_name_the_key_and_what_is_wrong_with_it(self):"
	SPEC "brigade collect <name> [key=value ...] [--since <n>d|<date>] resolves the collector, runs"
		+ "it through the process runner, writes its document and a sidecar holding the resolved"
		+ "command, the parameters, the duration in ms, the exit code and the cache key, and prints"
		+ "the summary and the path of the document, text and --json carrying schema_version;"
		+ "inside a run the two files go under <BRIGADE_RUN_DIR>/collect/<name>/; outside a run"
		+ "they are the cache entry of a cached document, and go under"
		+ "$XDG_STATE_HOME/brigade/collect/<name>/ for a document that is not cached"
		IMPL "brigade/commands/collect.py::def collect("
		IMPL "brigade/collecting/collect_document.py::def collect_document("
		IMPL "tests/unit/collecting/test_collect_document.py::def"
			+ "test_should_record_beside_the_cached_document_how_it_was_collected(self):"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_collect.py::class BrigadeCollectInsideARunTest(CollectTestCase):"
		IMPL "tests/unit/collecting/test_collect_document.py::def"
			+ "test_should_keep_a_document_fresh_at_each_call_in_the_state_directory(self):"
	SPEC "a collector that exits non-zero or prints no document validating is a failure naming the"
		+ "collector, the exit code and the last 20 lines of its stderr; collect exits 1"
		IMPL "brigade/collecting/collect_document.py::def _describe_failure(name: str, answer,"
			+ "reason: str) -> BrigadeError:"
		IMPL "tests/cli/test_collect.py::def"
			+ "test_should_name_the_collector_its_exit_code_and_the_last_twenty_lines_of_its_stderr(self):"
	SPEC "the cache lives under $XDG_CACHE_HOME/brigade/collectors/ and holds the document of a"
		+ "collector that declares cache true, which each built-in declares; a collector that"
		+ "declares nothing is never cached and is collected afresh on every call, inside a run or"
		+ "outside; the key is the resolved command, the parameters, since converted to a date, and"
		+ "the sha of HEAD of the project's repository for git-log, git-diff-stat, worktrees and"
		+ "corpus, the size of the ledger for ledger; a call whose key is in the cache answers from"
		+ "it and says so; a failure is never cached"
		IMPL "brigade/collecting/read_cache_input.py::def read_cache_input(name: str, project:"
			+ "Path, runtime: Runtime) -> str | int | None:"
		IMPL "brigade/collecting/collect_document.py::def _compute_cache_key(collector, inputs:"
			+ "CollectorInputs, cache_input) -> str:"
