			+ "test_should_record_the_steps_beyond_the_budget(self):"
		IMPL "tests/unit/runs/test_run_segments.py::def"
			+ "test_should_record_no_signal_for_the_steps_of_a_client_that_counts_none(self):"
	SPEC "signal.recorded gains the optional field steps, written on budget_exceeded alone and"
		+ "absent from every other signal, as DESC 1 of the decision declaring the ledger events"
		+ "states"
		IMPL "brigade/ledger/signal_recorded.py::steps: int | None = None"
		IMPL "tests/unit/ledger/test_signal_recorded.py::def"
			+ "test_should_write_back_the_steps_of_a_segment_over_its_budget(self):"
	SPEC "tests/cli runs brigade run as a subprocess with the fake client declaring step_count and"
		+ "reporting one step more than the budget and no error: the run ends done, exit 0, and the"
		+ "ledger holds the budget_exceeded signal with its steps and budget; at exactly the"
		+ "budget, no such signal"
		IMPL "tests/unit/runs/test_run_segments.py::def"
			+ "test_should_record_the_steps_beyond_the_budget(self):"
		IMPL "tests/unit/runs/test_run_segments.py::def"
			+ "test_should_record_no_signal_for_a_segment_at_exactly_its_budget(self):"
	SPEC "the pull request states the cause of 57 turns under --max-turns 50, established by a run"
		+ "of the client, num_turns counted otherwise than --max-turns or the cap not applied, and"
		+ "corrects the computation of max_turns at brigade/adapters/clients/claude_code.py:65 so"
		+ "that the step cap holds, or names the cause with its evidence when it lies in the"
		+ "client, the computation then unchanged"
