TASK B196
	TITLE "A task whose worktree holds uncommitted changes when its pull request falls behind is"
		+ "repaired before it is rebased"
	STATUS implemented
	DELIVERED_BY 188
	TYPE fix
	MILESTONE @MILESTONE.M1
	COMPONENT "tick"
	ROLE ada
	SPEC "a task whose pull request is behind its wave branch and whose worktree holds uncommitted"
		+ "changes to tracked files gets no RebaseTask: the tick launches in that worktree the"
		+ "repair run of TASK B18, check repair when a check fails and remediation otherwise,"
		+ "whatever its state among pr_open, verifying, verified, changes_requested and fixing,"
		+ "recorded as task.state fixing and counted as a repair round; where today"
		+ "brigade/tick/plan.py:184-187 plans the rebase, which git refuses at every tick"
		IMPL "brigade/tick/plan.py::if task.holds_uncommitted_changes:"
		IMPL "brigade/tick/build_snapshot.py::holds_uncommitted_changes=standing and"
			+ "has_uncommitted_changes("
		IMPL "brigade/git/has_uncommitted_changes.py::def has_uncommitted_changes("
		IMPL "tests/unit/tick/test_plan.py::def"
			+ "test_should_repair_rather_than_rebase_a_task_behind_whose_worktree_holds_uncommitted_changes(self):"
	SPEC "past POLICY.VERIFY_ROUNDS repair rounds such a task is parked with the reason of the"
		+ "rounds spent instead of a repair run; its worktree is never reset nor stashed"
		IMPL "tests/unit/tick/test_plan.py::def"
			+ "test_should_park_a_task_behind_holding_uncommitted_changes_whose_repair_rounds_are_spent(self):"
	SPEC "once its worktree holds no uncommitted change, a task whose pull request is behind is"
		+ "rebased by the next tick as TASK B143 sets"
		IMPL "brigade/tick/plan.py::return RebaseTask("
		IMPL "tests/unit/tick/test_plan.py::def"
			+ "test_should_rebase_a_task_whose_pull_request_is_behind_the_wave_branch_before_anything_else(self):"
	SPEC "tests/unit prove a repair run and no rebase planned for a worktree holding uncommitted"
		+ "changes behind its wave branch, in fixing and in pr_open, the parking past"
		+ "POLICY.VERIFY_ROUNDS, and a clean worktree behind still rebased; tests/cli gains no"
		+ "case, as DESC 4 of the decision ThePortableContractIsTheCommandLineAndNeutralFiles sets"
		IMPL "tests/unit/tick/test_build_snapshot_from_the_corpus.py::def"
			+ "test_should_tell_that_the_worktree_of_a_task_holds_uncommitted_changes(self):"
		IMPL "tests/unit/git/test_has_uncommitted_changes.py::def"
			+ "test_should_tell_whether_the_worktree_holds_changes_to_its_tracked_files(self):"
	AFTER @TASK.B143
	RATIONALE "since PR 182 the tick rebases a task branch behind its wave by git, and git refuses"
		+ "a worktree holding uncommitted changes; the rebase is decided before every other path of"
		+ "the task (brigade/tick/plan.py:184-187), so the repair that would finish the interrupted"
		+ "work is never planned and the refused rebase comes back at every tick"
		REF @TASK.B143
	RATIONALE "the resumption already exists: a run of fixing that pushed nothing has its repair"
		+ "run launched again in the same worktree, a round counted by task.state fixing and parked"
		+ "past POLICY.VERIFY_ROUNDS; the task lets it pass before the rebase and adds no mechanism"
		REF @TASK.B18
	RATIONALE "the worktree is left to the repair run, never cleaned: the uncommitted changes are"
		+ "the work of an interrupted run"
	SOURCE "review 5616826315 of PR 182, thread 4350364074: a build or remediate run that ends"
		+ "without committing leaves such a worktree, and a task in fixing is in REBASED_STATES"
	SOURCE "the user's rulings of 2026-10-22 in the refinement of B196: « je vois pas où est le pb"
		+ "de reprendre un worktree pour le terminer »; « Réparer avant rebaser (Recommended) »;"
		+ "outside fixing, « Je dirais pareil que fixing »; « AFTER B143 seul (Recommended) »; «"
		+ "Oui, todo »"

